    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444-a2">

                <pb facs="0644" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg550"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consuls of the Treaty
                            Powers to King Malietoa.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Apia, Samoa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-14"><hi rendition="#italic">April 14,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Afioga</hi>: In reply to the request which was
                    made to us at our meeting with you, we have the honor to inform your Afioga and
                    your Government that we are unanimously agreed in refusing our consent to the
                    importation of the 1,000 rifles and 50,000 cartridges.</p>
                <p>The consuls would remind the King and Government that the treaty powers have been
                    ready in the past to support the King and Government of Samoa when necessary,
                    and they will be as ready in the future to afford protection should occasion
                    arise. Before the consuls consider the advisability of issuing a proclamation,
                    they unanimously suggest that the Government should first notify to all Samoans
                    by proclamation that so far as the Government is concerned, there is peace in
                    Samoa, and all persons are free to come and go throughout Samoa on their lawful
                    business, but that large “malagas” are forbidden.</p>
                <p>We have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. B. Cusack-Smith</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Her Britannic Majesty’s Consul</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rose</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                    >Imperial German Consul</hi>.</item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Blacklock</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                    rendition="#italic">Vice-Consul-General, United States of
                                    America.</hi></item>
                        </list></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
